id: pm-gh1576
title: "GH-1576: guard SDK and CLI mutations with expected item revisions"
description: Reported read-decide-write races in extension consumers need an optional atomic expected-item-hash precondition checked at the mutation commit boundary. Preserve existing no-precondition behavior and distinguish this from mutation lease fencing.
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: concurrency,"gh:1576",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-24T16:12:40.963Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T16:12:40.963Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Define a public optional expected revision/hash contract across single-item and bulk SDK/CLI/MCP mutations; Check each precondition under the authoritative item lock at commit time and refuse stale writes without acknowledged item or history changes; Return typed current revision and bounded actionable change evidence; Deterministic concurrent controls cover closeout tags, collection cleanup, claim and bulk partial outcomes without weakening lease fencing."
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: A write based on a stale observed revision refuses atomically and supplies bounded recovery evidence.
